=== AR locale, same Milk category, re-confirmed 17:11:43 / 17:12:00 / 17:12:14 / 17:12:40 (multiple childes/category-wise-products refetches) ===
I/flutter ( 5147): type 'int' is not a subtype of type 'String?'
(same stack: ItemModel.fromJson item_model.dart:32:5)

Root cause (read, not touched by this ticket's diff):
  VendorApp/lib/features/store/domain/models/item_model.dart:32
    _offset = json['offset'];              // field declared `String? _offset`
  Backend always returns offset as an int:
    Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/Vendor/CategoryController.php:66,85
    Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/Vendor/ItemController.php:1194,1240 (and 1321,1345)
      $offset = max((int) ($request['offset'] ?? 1), 1); ... 'offset' => $offset,
  No try/catch anywhere in the await chain (CategoryRepository/StoreRepository ->
  Service -> Controller), so the thrown TypeError aborts the async fn after the
  await; _itemList/itemList stays null and _isLoading never flips to false ->
  the item-card list screen is stuck in its shimmer/skeleton state forever, for
  ANY category or "All Items" fetch, in either language.

Effect on this QA run: blocks a full-screen live render of ItemWidget/ItemRatingBadge
via both TL-named call sites. Component-level live verification instead via
`flutter test test/item_widget_rating_count_rtl_test.dart` (pumps the real,
unmocked ItemRatingBadge production widget) — see QA comment for detail.
